      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# CELL 16: DETAILED ANALYSIS AND INSIGHTS\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\"\"\n",
        "╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n",
        "║              ANALYSIS AND INSIGHTS                                  ║\n",
        "║              Dataset: Kaggle IMDB 50K Movie Reviews                 ║\n",
        "╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n",
        "\n",
        "DATASET:\n",
        "  Source: Kaggle (lakshmi25npathi/imdb-dataset-of-50k-movie-reviews)\n",
        "  Size:  50,000 movie reviews (25K positive + 25K negative)\n",
        "  Task:  Binary Sentiment Classification\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPERIMENT 1 — Full Fine-Tuning:\n",
        "  • All 109M+ BERT parameters trainable\n",
        "  • Best performance — model adapts all layers to task\n",
        "  • Most computationally expensive\n",
        "  • Risk of overfitting on small datasets\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPERIMENT 2 — Frozen BERT (Classifier Only):\n",
        "  • Only ~1,500 parameters trainable (classifier head)\n",
        "  • BERT used as fixed feature extractor\n",
        "  • Fastest training, lowest performance\n",
        "  • Pre-trained features may not align perfectly with task\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPERIMENT 3 — Last 2 Layers Fine-Tuned:\n",
        "  • ~14M parameters trainable (Layers 10-11 + pooler + classifier)\n",
        "  • Good balance of performance and compute cost\n",
